name: local-cr description: Review local changes against dev and report only real, actionable issues.

Local CR

Review the current branch against dev.

Scope

Use:

```bash
git status --short
git branch --show-current
git diff origin/dev...HEAD
git diff HEAD
```

If origin/dev does not exist, use:

```bash
git diff dev...HEAD
```

Review:

• committed changes in the current branch vs dev
• uncommitted local changes

Do not review unrelated legacy code.

What to check

Focus only on real issues:

• Bugs and regressions
• Null/undefined/runtime errors
• Missing await, bad async logic, race conditions
• TypeScript type/runtime mismatches
• NestJS DI, guards, DTO validation, API contracts
• React hooks, state, stale data, React Query mistakes
• SQL/ORM queries, transactions, N+1, schema mismatches
• Security/auth/authorization/input validation
• Meaningful performance problems
• Significant duplicated logic introduced by the change
• Edge cases and error handling
• Breaking changes to existing behavior or contracts
• SOLID/maintainability issues that materially increase bug risk
• Missing or incorrect logging for important failures
• Missing tests for important changed behavior

Ignore:

• formatting
• naming preferences
• minor refactors
• harmless style issues
• speculative findings

Verification

Before reporting a finding:

1. Read enough surrounding code to verify it.
2. Confirm the issue is caused by the current change.
3. Confirm another layer does not already handle it.
4. Report only if confidence is high.

Prefer a few strong findings over many weak ones.

Severity

Use:

• CRITICAL — security, data loss, outage, corruption
• HIGH — likely production bug/regression
• MEDIUM — real edge case or moderate issue
• LOW — rare, only if clearly actionable

Output

For each finding:

```text
[HIGH] Short title
File: path/to/file.ts:42

Problem:
What is wrong.

Impact:
What can actually happen.

Fix:
Smallest practical fix.
```

Finish with:

```text
Verdict: APPROVE
```

or:

```text
Verdict: CHANGES REQUESTED
```

Use CHANGES REQUESTED for any CRITICAL or HIGH issue.

If there are no real issues:

```text
No blocking issues found.
Verdict: APPROVE
```

Do not modify code unless explicitly asked.
Do not commit, push, or post comments.